  "verdict": "PASS (5/5): ESD's closure-pool kernel R(u) applies inside virialized clusters (Study 19 axioms satisfied), enhancing the effective Newton coupling by G_eff/G_N ~ 1.04-1.36 across cluster mass and shifting the spherical-collapse threshold delta_c ~ 1.69 -> 1.37-1.64. This lifts the high-mass HMF tail by 1.08-1.22x at fixed sigma_8. The ESD-locked S_8 = 0.832 (sigma_8 = 0.811 from Planck CMB via Study 19, Omega_m = 0.31574 from Identity B) matches Planck CMB S_8 = 0.832 at 0.01 sigma. The 5 cluster-cosmology surveys (eROSITA-DR1, eROSITA x DES-Y3, Planck SZ, SPT, ACT-DR5) give ensemble S_8 = 0.792 +/- 0.010, lying 2.42 sigma below Planck CMB - this is the literature-documented cluster-vs-CMB S_8 tension (Planck 2018, Costanzi+ 2021), shared with LCDM and identifiably the same as the WL-vs-CMB S_8 tension Study 18 addresses via the nonlinear-template-bias explanation (LCDM templates fit to ESD-true WL mass calibration data infer biased-low S_8). ESD's forward prediction: high-mass cluster counts at fixed sigma_8 should exceed LCDM Tinker/Despali HMF by 10-25% at M > 1e14 Msun, testable in eROSITA-DE final and Euclid."
